      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's unlikely that the issue is severe enough to warrant urgent care, and over-the-counter options like ibuprofen and muscle relaxants might help alleviate the discomfort. However, before taking any medication, try some gentle stretches to loosen up the muscles in your neck and jaw, such as a simple chin tuck or side-to-side neck stretch. If the pain persists or worsens, consult with your primary care physician or dentist to rule out any underlying issues.",
